{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, one second, the system's still loading. Right, come in.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): No rush. Absolutely tipping it down, I got soaked between the car park and the door.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grim, isn't it. The one-day game at Headingley got rained off as well.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): My brother's livid. Tickets, a plastic mac, two hours, and they never bowled a ball. He reckons the forecast was a stitch-up.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): They were going along nicely yesterday before it rolled in. Anyway, what's brought you?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh, it's nothing. I'm thirty weeks and my legs go all creepy at night. That's the only reason I'm here.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Creepy. Sorry, say that again, wrong letter open.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Creeping. Err, both legs, like something's crawling under the skin once I'm in bed, and I have to move them. Not a big deal.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks. Umm. Yeah, three weeks.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sleep ok?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Sleep's fine. Honestly.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does it hurt?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not painful.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Swollen ankles?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): It says asthma on here. Still a problem?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, for years. Salbutamol, the blue inhaler. I barely use it, it's nothing.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Nurse's numbers are on the screen. Blood pressure one nineteen over seventy-seven, no, sorry, one oh nine over seventy-seven, temperature thirty-eight point three, and weight fifty-two kilos.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Fifty-two, right. I don't feel hot.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Last time in March you were sixty-eight, that was the pulse, I was in the wrong column. Your last pressure was one-forty. Today's pulse is seventy-six. Do you feel feverish?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Never. I'm fine.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any cough?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): The asthma. Any chest tightness with it?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. If I leg it for the bus. Hardly ever, though.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Headache? Or being sick?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): No headache. Not that either.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Pain in the calf?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ferritin last week came back at nine. That's low, and it fits the creeping legs.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Nine. That's not dire. Probably nothing.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): It is low at this stage. Which tablets are you on? Sorry, screen's jumped, say it again.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Ferrus sulphate. Two hundred milligrams, once a day. And folic acid, four hundred micrograms, every morning.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Once a day on the iron, not twice? I lost you.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Once. I take it.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Good. Stay on both of them. Don't stop the iron just because the legs feel like nothing to you.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): If you say so. I do take them.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): Earlier you said sleep was fine. Was that right?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Well. I'm awake about two till five, shifting the legs. So I'm not really sleeping. I cope, though.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): That matters. Sounds like restless legs from the low iron. I'll put a repeat ferritin on the form, and the midwife check booked for next Thursday stays. Tell her about the legs and the temperature, and if you feel properly unwell before Thursday, ring maternity assessment.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): She texted about Thursday already. Yeah. I need to run, the meter's on twenty minutes."
 ],
